# This project needs no environment variables.
#
# file-organiser is a local CLI with no network calls, no database and no
# third-party accounts. There is nothing to configure here and no .env to
# create -- `uv sync` then `uv run file-organiser --help` is the whole setup.
#
# The file is kept so the repo layout matches the rest of the portfolio, and so
# it is obvious that the absence of secrets is deliberate rather than an
# oversight.
#
# Behaviour is configured per-run instead, with a TOML rules file:
#
#     uv run file-organiser organise ~/Downloads --config examples/rules.toml
